  "published": "2026-10-11T01:12:43.85Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- Fix CsvFileReader file-path constructors leaking the handle and ignoring Encoding.\n- CsvFileReader(string) now marks its StreamReader as internal, so Dispose closes the file.\n- Fixes.\n- Make the File.CSV mapper and type-converter caches thread-safe.\n- The static mapper and type-converter caches were plain Dictionary instances with no synchronisation, so readers or writers for the same record type used on different threads could corrupt them or throw on a duplicate key.\n- TypeConverterCache is now a ConcurrentDictionary.\n- RegisterMapper checked for typeof(TMapper) but added under typeof(TRecordLine), so a second registration threw.\n- The reader and writer reference pages now describe thread safety.\n- Fix CsvFileWriter file-path constructor throwing IOException when Encoding is set.\n- CsvFileWriter(string, CsvFileOptions) no longer chains to the single-argument path constructor.\n- Throw ObjectDisposedException when CsvFileReader/CsvFileWriter are used after Dispose.\n- CsvFileIoBase now tracks disposal through private protected helpers, and each reader and writer sets the flag in Dispose.",
